From: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: boot-mode: defer RockUSB to preboot

Starting RockUSB directly from board_late_init is too early for reliable
RK3588 gadget enumeration. Follow the existing fastboot and UMS pattern:
schedule the command in preboot and let main_loop start it after board
initialization is complete.

Signed-off-by: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c | 11 ++---------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -83,15 +83,8 @@ __weak int rockchip_dnl_key_pressed(void)
 
 void rockchip_dnl_mode_check(void)
 {
-	int ret;
-
 	if (rockchip_dnl_key_pressed()) {
-		printf("download key pressed, entering RockUSB loader mode...\n");
-		ret = run_command("rockusb 0 mmc 0", 0);
-		if (!ret)
-			return;
-		printf("RockUSB unavailable, falling back to BootROM download mode...\n");
-		set_back_to_bootrom_dnl_flag();
-		do_reset(NULL, 0, 0, NULL);
+		printf("download key pressed, scheduling RockUSB loader mode...\n");
+		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; rockusb 0 mmc 0");
 	}
 }
